#
# Counter-example for math:HomomorphicEncryptionSchemeShape: a scheme that declares its
# homomorphic operation, its preservation law, and its security assumption but omits its
# math:noiseModel (sh:minCount 1), so validation MUST emit
# shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent (and no other finding). It declares math:preservedOperation
# and math:preservationLaw so the HomomorphismShape / PreservationLawShape are satisfied,
# isolating the noise-model violation.
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecHeMissingNoiseModel).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:noiselessHe a math:HomomorphicEncryptionScheme ;
    math:preservedOperation ex:ctMul ;
    math:homomorphicOver ex:ctMul ;
    math:preservationLaw ex:heLaw ;
    math:securityAssumption math:ringLearningWithErrors .

ex:ctMul a math:Operation .
